# 🔐 Environment Variables Configuration

## Server (.env)

```bash
# Database
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://user:password@cluster.mongodb.net/thrive

# JWT
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret_key_here
JWT_EXPIRATION=7d

# Email (for OTP)
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=your_email@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=your_app_password

# Google OAuth
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_client_id
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_google_client_secret
GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=https://health-thrive.site/auth/google/callback

# Facebook OAuth
FACEBOOK_APP_ID=your_facebook_app_id
FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET=your_facebook_app_secret
FACEBOOK_CALLBACK_URL=https://health-thrive.site/auth/facebook/callback

# AI - GEMINI API (NEW - Required for AI Recommendations)
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# API Base
API_PORT=3001
API_URL=https://health-thrive.site
```

## Client (.env.local)

```bash
# API Configuration
VITE_API_URL=https://health-thrive.site
```

---

## 🤖 Setting up Gemini API Key

### Step 1: Get API Key
1. Go to [Google AI Studio](https://makersuite.google.com/app/apikey)
2. Click "Get API Key"
3. Create a new API key
4. Copy the key

### Step 2: Add to .env
```bash
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_copied_key_here
```

### Step 3: Restart Server
```bash
npm run start:dev
```

---

## 📝 Notes

- **GEMINI_API_KEY** is required for AI-powered recommendation features
- Keep all sensitive keys in `.env` file (not in version control)
- Use `.env.example` as template for new developers
- Never commit `.env` files to Git

---

## 🚀 Deployment

### Production Environment Variables
Set these on your hosting platform (Vercel, Railway, Heroku, etc.):
- All variables from `.env`
- Update URLs to production domain
- Use production API keys

### Example for Railway/Vercel
```
MONGODB_URI=<production_db_url>
JWT_SECRET=<strong_random_secret>
GEMINI_API_KEY=<api_key>
API_URL=https://your-production-domain.com
```
